# On-device classifiers. Nothing here is on by default.

config ULTRAWIDELOCK_ML_LOS
	bool "Line-of-sight / obstructed classifier from DW3000 receive diagnostics"
	help
	  Compile the decision tree that says whether the direct path between the
	  reader and the phone is obstructed, from the receiver's own diagnostics
	  rather than from the ranging distance. An obstructed 1 m and a clear 3 m
	  produce similar time-of-flight estimates and do not mean the same thing.

	  MEASURED on arm-none-eabi-gcc 16.1.0 for Cortex-M4F at -Os, per section:

	    ultrawidelock_ml_los_classify        236 B   quantise + call, scaler folded in
	    the tree                    74 B   2 integer comparisons
	    range correction           120 B   20*log10(d) without libm
	    its log2 table              36 B   .rodata, 9 x float32
	    ----------------------------------
	    classifier                 466 B
	    ultrawidelock_ml_los_fp_resid         16 B   only if called
	    ultrawidelock_ml_los_vendor           20 B   only if called
	    ultrawidelock_ml_los_disagrees        32 B   only if called

	  There is no separate scaler in .rodata any more: at two features GCC folds
	  lo[] and scale[] into ultrawidelock_ml_los_classify as immediates, which is why that
	  function grew from 152 B while the 32 B array disappeared.

	  and 0 B of RAM: .data and .bss are both empty. There is no arena, no
	  interpreter and no allocation, so there is nothing to fail at init and
	  nothing to size. The only runtime cost is 28 B of stack for the quantised
	  feature vector. 466 B is 0.9% of the shipping image's free flash.

	  The model is a decision tree because that won a measured bake-off against
	  an int8 TensorFlow Lite Micro network and a random forest, on accuracy
	  per byte. It is also the only one of
	  the three whose generated C can be proved identical to the model that was
	  trained, which is why the host suite can certify it rather than merely
	  regression-pin it. Depth 2 rather than the 4 the public set preferred:
	  on this board's captures a deeper tree scores worse on every split that
	  holds out a whole capture (0.7729 at depth 2, 0.7310 at 3, 0.7011 at 4).

	  TWO FEATURES, AND ONE OF THEM IS NOT A RAW REGISTER. fp_resid is
	  first-path power with free-space spreading at the measured range removed,
	  fp_pwr + 20*log10(d / 1 m). An obstructed 1 m and a clear 3 m produce
	  similar absolute power, which is this classifier's founding problem, and
	  it is only a problem while the model does not know which of the two it is
	  looking at. Worth +13.5 points over the four absolute features on the
	  strictest split available, at two fewer features (RESULTS.md Result 11).
	  The log is a nine-entry table and a leading-bit exponent rather than
	  log10f, so this module still links no libc: `arm-none-eabi-nm -u` on it
	  reports not one undefined symbol.

	  EVERYTHING IT NEEDS, THE HARDWARE ALREADY PRODUCES. rx_pwr and the fp_pwr
	  behind fp_resid come from dwt_readdiagnostics alone (ipatovPower,
	  ipatovF1..F3, ipatovAccumCount) and the range comes from the DS-TWR round
	  the reader already completes. The ten channel-shape features the public
	  set offered need the 64-tap CIR window, and on the DWM3001CDK an image
	  that reads the accumulator cannot range at all, so a seam wanting them
	  would be an API firmware could never call (RESULTS.md Result 7).

	  THE RANGE MAY LAG BY A ROUND. A DS-TWR round yields its distance when the
	  round completes while diagnostics are read per reception, so a caller
	  classifying every reception holds the previous round's range. That is
	  also what the training data measured, since the captured range came from
	  a status line printed every ~2 s, so a lagged range is the case the
	  numbers above are about rather than an approximation of it.

	  ENABLING THIS LINKS THE CLASSIFIER, NOT A DECISION. Nothing in the
	  ranging path calls it, and the feature extractor that would turn a
	  dwt_rxdiag_t into those four floats is unwritten.

	  THE THRESHOLDS ARE THIS BOARD'S, from 556 walk-up receptions captured on
	  a DWM3001CDK against an iPhone: 267 unobstructed over two sessions and
	  289 with the phone shielded by the wearer's body over two geometries
	  (held behind the back and carried in a back pocket, d = +0.06 on fp_pwr
	  between them). Balanced accuracy 0.8505 +/- 0.0302 over 5-fold
	  cross-validation repeated ten times on the four absolute features, and
	  0.8800 +/- 0.0251 for the two shipped, against 0.7431 +/- 0.0359 for
	  Decawave's own rule refit on the same data: RESULTS.md Results 9 and 11.
	  Twelve of those receptions carry no usable range and are dropped when the
	  residual is used, so the shipped model is fitted on 544 of the 556.

	  BOTH SIDES GENERALISE, and that is measured rather than assumed. Holding
	  out a whole capture entirely, the shipped pair scores 0.7729 against
	  0.6381 for the four absolute features, and both clear the 0.7431 vendor
	  floor. The unobstructed sessions are NOT identical: d = +0.69 on fp_pwr
	  between two an hour apart, about 2.9 dB, roughly a third of the
	  obstruction signal itself. Taking the range out of the power is what
	  most of the +13.5 points is buying back. Session drift is still real and
	  is why to retrain at an install rather than treat these as universal.

	  WHAT THAT DOES NOT COVER. One room, one phone, one person, one day. The
	  generation gates below are also weaker than they read: sized for the
	  public set's 42,000 samples, they now run on 544, which leaves 82 in the
	  held-out split. They still prove the generated C is the model that was
	  trained; they prove it over far less ground. Recapture at any install
	  whose geometry differs, which at 466 B is cheaper than transferring.

if ULTRAWIDELOCK_ML_LOS

module = ULTRAWIDELOCK_ML
module-str = ultrawidelock_ml
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endif # ULTRAWIDELOCK_ML_LOS
